{"id":"mahabharata-6-019","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":19,"title":"एकोनविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 19 · The Pandava array","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how the Pandavas faced the larger army with a smaller one. Sanjaya describes Yudhishthira's formation under Dhrishtadyumna, with Bhima in front and Arjuna's chariot guided by Krishna.","kn":"ಚಿಕ್ಕ ಸೈನ್ಯದಿಂದ ಪಾಂಡವರು ದೊಡ್ಡ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ಎದುರಿಸಿದರೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನನ ನೇತೃತ್ವದ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ವ್ಯೂಹ, ಮುಂದೆ ಭೀಮ, ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಸಾರಥಿಯಾದ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ರಥವನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि पाण्डवों ने छोटी सेना से बड़ी सेना का सामना कैसे किया। संजय धृष्टद्युम्न के नेतृत्व में युधिष्ठिर के व्यूह, आगे भीम और कृष्ण द्वारा संचालित अर्जुन के रथ का वर्णन करते हैं।","te":"చిన్న సైన్యంతో పాండవులు పెద్ద సైన్యాన్ని ఎలా ఎదుర్కొన్నారని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుని నాయకత్వంలో యుధిష్ఠిరుని వ్యూహం, ముందు భీముడు, కృష్ణుడు సారథిగా అర్జునుని రథాన్ని సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"சிறிய படையுடன் பாண்டவர்கள் பெரிய படையை எவ்வாறு எதிர்கொண்டனர் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னன் தலைமையில் யுதிஷ்டிரரின் அணிவகுப்பு, முன்னால் பீமன், கண்ணன் செலுத்தும் அர்ஜுனனின் தேரைச் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான்.","ml":"വലിയ സേനയെ ചെറിയ സേനകൊണ്ട് പാണ്ഡവർ എങ്ങനെ നേരിട്ടു എന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നന്റെ നേതൃത്വത്തിലുള്ള യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ വ്യൂഹത്തെ സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; മുന്നിൽ ഭീമൻ, കൃഷ്ണൻ തെളിക്കുന്ന അർജുനന്റെ രഥം."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.19; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्गीतापर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadgita Parva","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अक्षौहिण्यो दशैकां च व्यूढां दृष्ट्वा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nकथमल्पेन सैन्येन प्रत्यव्यूहत पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the eleven akshauhinis arrayed, how did Yudhishthira the Pandava array his small army against them?"}},{"n":2,"text":"यो वेद मानुषं व्यूहं दैवं गान्धर्वमासुरम् ।\nकथं भीष्मं स कौन्तेयः प्रत्यव्यूहत पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did the Pandava, son of Kunti, who knows the human, divine, Gandharva and Asura formations, array against Bhishma?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्राण्यनीकानि दृष्ट्वा व्यूढानि पाण्डवः ।\nअभ्यभाषत धर्मात्मा धर्मराजो धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Dhritarashtra armies arrayed, the Pandava Dharmaraja, righteous in soul, spoke to Dhananjaya."}},{"n":4,"text":"महर्षेर्वचनात्तात वेदयन्ति बृहस्पतेः ।\nसंहतान्योधयेदल्पान्कामं विस्तारयेद्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dear one, they report the saying of the great sage Brihaspati: a small force should fight in a compact mass, and a large one may spread out as it likes.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"सूचीमुखमनीकं स्यादल्पानां बहुभिः सह ।\nअस्माकं च तथा सैन्यमल्पीयः सुतरां परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"An army of few against many should have the needle-point form, and our army is far smaller than the enemy's.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"एतद्वचनमाज्ञाय महर्षेर्व्यूह पाण्डव ।\nतच्छ्रुत्वा धर्मराजस्य प्रत्यभाषत फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Knowing this word of the great sage, array the formation, Pandava.\" Hearing Dharmaraja, Phalguna replied."}},{"n":7,"text":"एष व्यूहामि ते राजन्व्यूहं परमदुर्जयम् ।\nअचलं नाम वज्राख्यं विहितं वज्रपाणिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King, I shall array for you this formation, very hard to conquer, called Achala, or Vajra, devised by the wielder of the thunderbolt.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"यः स वात इवोद्धूतः समरे दुःसहः परैः ।\nस नः पुरो योत्स्यति वै भीमः प्रहरतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhima, best of fighters, who is like a gale and unbearable to the enemy in battle, will fight in front of us.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तेजांसि रिपुसैन्यानां मृद्नन्पुरुषसत्तमः ।\nअग्रेऽग्रणीर्यास्यति नो युद्धोपायविचक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That best of men, trampling the strength of the enemy's armies and skilled in the means of war, will go at our front as leader.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"यं दृष्ट्वा पार्थिवाः सर्वे दुर्योधनपुरोगमाः ।\nनिवर्तिष्यन्ति संभ्रान्ताः सिंहं क्षुद्रमृगा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing him, all the kings with Duryodhana in front will turn back in confusion, like small beasts before a lion.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"तं सर्वे संश्रयिष्यामः प्राकारमकुतोभयम् ।\nभीमं प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठं वज्रपाणिमिवामराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We shall all take refuge in Bhima, best of fighters, as in a rampart safe from every side, as the immortals do in the thunderbolt-wielder.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"न हि सोऽस्ति पुमाँल्लोके यः संक्रुद्धं वृकोदरम् ।\nद्रष्टुमत्युग्रकर्माणं विषहेत नरर्षभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is no man in the world who could bear to look at the enraged Vrikodara, bull among men, of fearful deeds.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"भीमसेनो गदां बिभ्रद्वज्रसारमयीं दृढाम् ।\nचरन्वेगेन महता समुद्रमपि शोषयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhimasena, bearing his firm mace of thunderbolt-hard steel and moving with great speed, could even dry up the ocean.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"केकया धृष्टकेतुश्च चेकितानश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nएत तिष्ठन्ति सामात्याः प्रेक्षकास्ते नरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Kekayas, Dhrishtaketu and the mighty Chekitana, with their ministers, king, stand as onlookers.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रस्य दायादा इति बीभत्सुरब्रवीत् ।\nब्रुवाणं तु तथा पार्थं सर्वसैन्यानि मारिष ।\nअपूजयंस्तदा वाग्भिरनुकूलाभिराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They are Dhritarashtra's heirs,\" said Bibhatsu; and as Partha spoke so, all the armies, good sir, honoured him then in the battle with pleasant words."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा महाबाहुस्तथा चक्रे धनंजयः ।\nव्यूह्य तानि बलान्याशु प्रययौ फल्गुनस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus, the mighty-armed Dhananjaya did so, and Phalguna quickly arrayed those forces and set out."}},{"n":17,"text":"संप्रयातान्कुरून्दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवानां महाचमूः ।\nगङ्गेव पूर्णा स्तिमिता स्यन्दमाना व्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Kurus advance, the great army of the Pandavas appeared like the Ganga, full, still, yet flowing."}},{"n":18,"text":"भीमसेनोऽग्रणीस्तेषां धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च धृष्टकेतुश्च वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, Dhrishtadyumna son of Prishata, Nakula, Sahadeva and the mighty Dhrishtaketu were their leaders."}},{"n":19,"text":"समुद्योज्य ततः पश्चाद्राजाप्यक्षौहिणीवृतः ।\nभ्रातृभिः सह पुत्रैश्च सोऽभ्यरक्षत पृष्ठतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king, surrounded by an akshauhini, set his army in motion and guarded the rear, with his brothers and sons."}},{"n":20,"text":"चक्ररक्षौ तु भीमस्य माद्रीपुत्रौ महाद्युती ।\nद्रौपदेयाः ससौभद्राः पृष्ठगोपास्तरस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two splendid sons of Madri guarded Bhima's wheels, and the sons of Draupadi with Subhadra's son were the swift guards of the rear."}},{"n":21,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पाञ्चाल्यस्तेषां गोप्ता महारथः ।\nसहितः पृतनाशूरै रथमुख्यैः प्रभद्रकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna the Panchala, a great chariot-warrior, was their protector, together with the Prabhadrakas, army heroes and best of chariot-fighters."}},{"n":22,"text":"शिखण्डी तु ततः पश्चादर्जुनेनाभिरक्षितः ।\nयत्तो भीष्मविनाशाय प्रययौ भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, best of the Bharatas, Shikhandin, guarded by Arjuna, went behind, eager for Bhishma's destruction."}},{"n":23,"text":"पृष्ठगोपोऽर्जुनस्यापि युयुधानो महारथः ।\nचक्ररक्षौ तु पाञ्चाल्यौ युधामन्यूत्तमौजसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yuyudhana, the great chariot-warrior, was Arjuna's rear guard, and the two Panchalas, Yudhamanyu and Uttamauja, guarded his wheels."}},{"n":24,"text":"राजा तु मध्यमानीके कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nबृहद्भिः कुञ्जरैर्मत्तैश्चलद्भिरचलैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the central division, King Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, stood with great, rutting elephants moving like mountains."}},{"n":25,"text":"अक्षौहिण्या च पाञ्चाल्यो यज्ञसेनो महामनाः ।\nविराटमन्वयात्पश्चात्पाण्डवार्थे पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The high-minded Panchala Yajnasena, the valiant, followed Virata with an akshauhini for the Pandavas' cause."}},{"n":26,"text":"तेषामादित्यचन्द्राभाः कनकोत्तमभूषणाः ।\nनानाचिह्नधरा राजन्रथेष्वासन्महाध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their great banners, bright as the sun and moon, with the finest golden ornaments, bore many emblems on their chariots, King."}},{"n":27,"text":"समुत्सर्प्य ततः पश्चाद्धृष्टद्युम्नो महारथः ।\nभ्रातृभिः सह पुत्रैश्च सोऽभ्यरक्षद्युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great chariot-warrior Dhrishtadyumna, going forward, guarded Yudhishthira with his brothers and sons."}},{"n":28,"text":"त्वदीयानां परेषां च रथेषु विविधान्ध्वजान् ।\nअभिभूयार्जुनस्यैको ध्वजस्तस्थौ महाकपिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the many banners on the chariots of both your side and the enemy's, only Arjuna's banner with the great monkey stood out, overpowering the rest."}},{"n":29,"text":"पादातास्त्वग्रतोऽगच्छन्नसिशक्त्यृष्टिपाणयः ।\nअनेकशतसाहस्रा भीमसेनस्य रक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Foot soldiers with swords, javelins and lances in hand went in front, many hundreds of thousands, as guards of Bhimasena."}},{"n":30,"text":"वारणा दशसाहस्राः प्रभिन्नकरटामुखाः ।\nशूरा हेममयैर्जालैर्दीप्यमाना इवाचलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were ten thousand elephants with rut flowing from their temples, brave and shining in golden nets like mountains."}},{"n":31,"text":"क्षरन्त इव जीमूता मदार्द्राः पद्मगन्धिनः ।\nराजानमन्वयुः पश्चाच्चलन्त इव पर्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like clouds raining, moist with rut and fragrant as lotuses, they followed the king, moving like mountains."}},{"n":32,"text":"भीमसेनो गदां भीमां प्रकर्षन्परिघोपमाम् ।\nप्रचकर्ष महत्सैन्यं दुराधर्षो महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-minded Bhimasena, hard to withstand, dragged along his terrible mace, like an iron bar, and drew the great army."}},{"n":33,"text":"तमर्कमिव दुष्प्रेक्ष्यं तपन्तं रश्मिमालिनम् ।\nन शेकुः सर्वतो योधाः प्रतिवीक्षितुमन्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warriors on every side could not look at him near, burning like the sun with his garland of rays."}},{"n":34,"text":"वज्रो नामैष तु व्यूहो दुर्भिदः सर्वतोमुखः ।\nचापविद्युद्ध्वजो घोरो गुप्तो गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"This formation, named Vajra, is hard to break, faces every side, has a bow and lightning for its banners, is terrible, and is guarded by the bearer of Gandiva."}},{"n":35,"text":"यं प्रतिव्यूह्य तिष्ठन्ति पाण्डवास्तव वाहिनीम् ।\nअजेयो मानुषे लोके पाण्डवैरभिरक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas stood arrayed against your army in it, invincible in the human world, protected by the Pandavas."}},{"n":36,"text":"संध्यां तिष्ठत्सु सैन्येषु सूर्यस्योदयनं प्रति ।\nप्रावात्सपृषतो वायुरनभ्रे स्तनयित्नुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the armies stood at dawn, toward the rising of the sun, a wind blew with drops of rain, and there was thunder without clouds."}},{"n":37,"text":"विष्वग्वाताश्च वान्त्युग्रा नीचैः शर्करकर्षिणः ।\nरजश्चोद्धूयमानं तु तमसाच्छादयज्जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fierce winds blew from every side, low, dragging gravel, and the raised dust covered the world in darkness."}},{"n":38,"text":"पपात महती चोल्का प्राङ्मुखी भरतर्षभ ।\nउद्यन्तं सूर्यमाहत्य व्यशीर्यत महास्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, a great meteor fell facing east, struck the rising sun and shattered with a great sound."}},{"n":39,"text":"अथ सज्जीयमानेषु सैन्येषु भरतर्षभ ।\nनिष्प्रभोऽभ्युदियात्सूर्यः सघोषो भूश्चचाल ह ।\nव्यशीर्यत सनादा च तदा भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, best of the Bharatas, while the armies were getting ready, the sun rose without brightness, the earth shook with a roar and split with a rumble."}},{"n":40,"text":"निर्घाता बहवो राजन्दिक्षु सर्वासु चाभवन् ।\nप्रादुरासीद्रजस्तीव्रं न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, there were many thunderclaps in all directions, a thick dust arose and nothing could be seen."}},{"n":41,"text":"ध्वजानां धूयमानानां सहसा मातरिश्वना ।\nकिङ्किणीजालनद्धानां काञ्चनस्रग्वतां रवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the great banners with flags and the splendour of the sun, shaken suddenly by the wind, covered with nets of bells and wearing golden garlands, rang with their sounds."}},{"n":42,"text":"महतां सपताकानामादित्यसमतेजसाम् ।\nसर्वं झणझणीभूतमासीत्तालवनेष्विव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everything seemed to rattle and tinkle as in groves of palms."}},{"n":43,"text":"एवं ते पुरुषव्याघ्राः पाण्डवा युद्धनन्दिनः ।\nव्यवस्थिताः प्रतिव्यूह्य तव पुत्रस्य वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus those tigers among men, the Pandavas, delighting in battle, stood arrayed against your son's army."}},{"n":44,"text":"स्रंसन्त इव मज्जानो योधानां भरतर्षभ ।\nदृष्ट्वाग्रतो भीमसेनं गदापाणिमवस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, the marrow of the warriors seemed to melt when they saw Bhimasena standing in front with the mace in his hand."}}]}]}